@page
@model IndexModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Stop maintaining reports";
    ViewData["PageKey"] = "home";
    ViewData["Description"] = "Someone needs a report, a developer owns it forever. Let people ask instead — answered by a model on your own hardware, bounded by the permissions you already wrote.";
}

@section Head {
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="~/css/home.css" />
}

@* [00] Boot. Decorative: it is aria-hidden and removed entirely under reduced motion.
   The hero below renders immediately underneath, so the headline is readable whether or not
   this ever runs. *@
<div class="boot" id="boot" aria-hidden="true" hidden>
    <div class="boot__inner">
        <div class="boot__lines" id="boot-lines"></div>
        <div class="boot__meter"><span class="boot__meter-fill" id="boot-fill"></span></div>
        <div class="boot__pct"><span id="boot-pct">000</span>%</div>
    </div>
    <button type="button" class="boot__skip" id="boot-skip">Skip <kbd>esc</kbd></button>
</div>

@* The signature scene. Fixed behind sections 01–05, lazily loaded, replaced by a static
   drawing on small screens, low-power devices, or when motion is reduced. *@
<div class="scene" aria-hidden="true">
    <canvas id="schema-canvas" class="scene__canvas"></canvas>
    <div class="scene__fallback" id="scene-fallback"></div>
</div>

<!-- ───────────────────────────── [01] HERO ───────────────────────────── -->
<section class="hero" id="s01" data-section="01">
    <div class="shell hero__inner">
        <p class="label"><span class="label__index">[01]</span> The premise</p>

        <h1 class="hero__headline" data-split>
            Stop maintaining reports.<br />
            Start answering questions.
        </h1>

        <p class="hero__sub">
            Every report starts as a favour and ends as a dependency. The data is already in your
            database — so let people ask it directly, and let the rules you already wrote decide
            what comes back.
        </p>

        <div class="hero__actions">
            <a class="btn" href="/reports" data-magnetic>
                Open the workspace <span class="btn__arrow">→</span>
            </a>
            <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="#s04" data-magnetic>See how it's governed</a>
        </div>

        <ul class="pillars">
            <li class="pillar">
                <span class="label"><span class="label__index">01</span></span>
                <h2>No more report tickets</h2>
                <p>A question, not a work item. Nobody inherits a PDF generator.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="pillar">
                <span class="label"><span class="label__index">02</span></span>
                <h2>Rules you already wrote</h2>
                <p>Roles and row policies that already exist decide what the answer contains.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="pillar">
                <span class="label"><span class="label__index">03</span></span>
                <h2>Your data never leaves</h2>
                <p>The model runs on your hardware. Nothing is sent anywhere to be read.</p>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- ───────────────────────────── [02] PROBLEM ───────────────────────────── -->
<section class="band" id="s02" data-section="02">
    <div class="shell">
        <p class="label"><span class="label__index">[02]</span> The problem</p>
        <h2 class="band__headline" data-split>
            Someone needs a report.<br />Now a developer owns it forever.
        </h2>

        <ul class="cards">
            <li class="card" data-reveal>
                <span class="card__index">01</span>
                <h3>Fragile</h3>
                <p>A column gets renamed. The export breaks silently and nobody notices for a quarter.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="card" data-reveal>
                <span class="card__index">02</span>
                <h3>Stale</h3>
                <p>It answers the question someone had in March, not the one they have now.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="card" data-reveal>
                <span class="card__index">03</span>
                <h3>Backlogged</h3>
                <p>Every variation is a ticket. The queue is measured in weeks, the question in minutes.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="card" data-reveal>
                <span class="card__index">04</span>
                <h3>Bespoke</h3>
                <p>Forty reports, forty shapes, forty ways to be subtly wrong about the same number.</p>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- ───────────────────────────── [03] THE ASK ───────────────────────────── -->
<section class="band band--tall" id="s03" data-section="03">
    <div class="shell band__narrow">
        <p class="label"><span class="label__index">[03]</span> The ask</p>
        <h2 class="band__headline" data-split>Ask it the way you'd ask a colleague.</h2>
        <p class="band__lede">
            No query language, no report builder, no ticket. The model's job is only to decide
            <em>which</em> known measure you meant — never to write the query.
        </p>

        <div class="ask-field" data-reveal>
            <span class="ask-field__caret">&gt;</span>
            <span class="ask-field__text" id="ask-typed">revenue by region, last quarter</span>
            <span class="ask-field__cursor" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- ───────────────────────────── [04] THE GUARD ───────────────────────────── -->
<section class="band band--guard" id="s04" data-section="04">
    <div class="shell">
        <p class="label label--signal"><span class="label__index">[04]</span> The guard</p>
        <h2 class="band__headline" data-split>
            It can only answer what you<br />already let them see.
        </h2>
        <p class="band__lede">
            The same question, asked by three people. Nothing about the question changes — only
            who is asking. Pick one.
        </p>

        <div class="guard" data-reveal>
            <div class="guard__roles" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Ask as">
                <button type="button" class="role" role="radio" aria-checked="true" data-role="analyst">
                    <span class="role__name">Dana</span>
                    <span class="role__title">Analyst</span>
                </button>
                <button type="button" class="role" role="radio" aria-checked="false" data-role="regional_manager">
                    <span class="role__name">Marcus</span>
                    <span class="role__title">Regional Manager, North</span>
                </button>
                <button type="button" class="role" role="radio" aria-checked="false" data-role="hr_director">
                    <span class="role__name">Priya</span>
                    <span class="role__title">HR Director</span>
                </button>
            </div>

            <div class="guard__panels">
                @* Two questions side by side: one everyone may ask, one most may not. *@
                <article class="guard__panel">
                    <header class="guard__panel-head">
                        <span class="label">Question A</span>
                        <code>revenue by region, last quarter</code>
                    </header>
                    <table class="guard__table">
                        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Region</th><th scope="col">Revenue</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody id="guard-rows-a"></tbody>
                    </table>
                    <p class="guard__note" id="guard-note-a"></p>
                </article>

                <article class="guard__panel">
                    <header class="guard__panel-head">
                        <span class="label">Question B</span>
                        <code>average salary by department</code>
                    </header>
                    <table class="guard__table">
                        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Department</th><th scope="col">Average</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody id="guard-rows-b"></tbody>
                    </table>
                    <p class="guard__note" id="guard-note-b"></p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </div>

        <p class="band__footnote">
            Two separate mechanisms. The policy engine refuses the measure and says why; Postgres
            row-level security bounds the rows underneath, so even a bug above it returns nothing
            extra.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- ───────────────────────────── [05] THE RESULT ───────────────────────────── -->
<section class="band" id="s05" data-section="05">
    <div class="shell band__narrow">
        <p class="label"><span class="label__index">[05]</span> The result</p>
        <h2 class="band__headline" data-split>A report that shows its working.</h2>
        <p class="band__lede">
            Every answer carries the query that produced it, the tables it read, and anything held
            back. A number you can't trace is a number you can't use.
        </p>

        <figure class="provenance" data-reveal>
            <figcaption class="label">Provenance · read</figcaption>
            <p><code>orders</code> <code>order_items</code> <code>regions</code> <code>products</code></p>
            <figcaption class="label">Withheld</figcaption>
            <p><code class="is-withheld">compensation.annual_salary</code> — restricted to HR Director</p>
        </figure>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- ───────────────────────────── [06] LOCAL ───────────────────────────── -->
<section class="band band--quiet" id="s06" data-section="06">
    <div class="shell band__narrow">
        <p class="label"><span class="label__index">[06]</span> Where it runs</p>
        <h2 class="band__headline" data-split>The model runs on your hardware.</h2>
        <p class="band__lede">
            Questions and schema stay on the machine. The planner speaks to a local server —
            Ollama, LM Studio, llama.cpp — and the compiled query never leaves the network it
            was always on.
        </p>

        <ol class="flow" data-reveal>
            <li class="flow__node">Question</li>
            <li class="flow__arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</li>
            <li class="flow__node flow__node--signal">Local model</li>
            <li class="flow__arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</li>
            <li class="flow__node">Your database</li>
            <li class="flow__cut" aria-hidden="true"></li>
            <li class="flow__node flow__node--off">The internet</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- ───────────────────────────── [07] HOW ───────────────────────────── -->
<section class="band" id="s07" data-section="07">
    <div class="shell">
        <p class="label"><span class="label__index">[07]</span> How it works</p>
        <h2 class="band__headline" data-split>Four steps, one of them non-negotiable.</h2>

        <ol class="steps">
            <li class="step" data-reveal>
                <span class="step__index">01</span>
                <h3>Ask</h3>
                <p>A question in plain language, from whoever needs the answer.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="step" data-reveal>
                <span class="step__index">02</span>
                <h3>Plan</h3>
                <p>The model picks measures and groupings from a catalog. It sees keys, not a schema.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="step" data-reveal>
                <span class="step__index">03</span>
                <h3>Guard</h3>
                <p>The plan is validated against that catalog, then authorized for the person asking.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="step" data-reveal>
                <span class="step__index">04</span>
                <h3>Compile</h3>
                <p>The server builds parameterized SQL from its own metadata. The model never writes SQL.</p>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- ───────────────────────────── [08] CTA ───────────────────────────── -->
<section class="band band--cta" id="s08" data-section="08">
    <div class="shell band__narrow">
        <h2 class="cta__headline" data-split>Ask it something.</h2>
        <p class="band__lede">
            Three identities are seeded. Ask all three the same thing and watch the answers differ.
        </p>
        <a class="btn" href="/reports" data-magnetic>Open the workspace <span class="btn__arrow">→</span></a>
    </div>
</section>

@section Scripts {
    <script src="~/lib/gsap/gsap.min.js" defer></script>
    <script src="~/lib/gsap/ScrollTrigger.min.js" defer></script>
    <script src="~/lib/gsap/SplitText.min.js" defer></script>
    <script src="~/lib/gsap/CustomEase.min.js" defer></script>
    <script src="~/lib/lenis/lenis.min.js" defer></script>
    <script type="module" src="~/js/home/index.js"></script>
}
